<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/page">
<$fill $name="body">

!! Plugin files

|!File |!Type |!Role |
|`widgets/json-obj.js` |`widget` |`<$json-obj>` — creates JSON object, manages builder context |
|`widgets/json-array.js` |`widget` |`<$json-array>` — creates JSON array, supports scalar mode via `filter` + `type` |
|`widgets/json-prop.js` |`widget` |`<$json-prop>` — sets key/value on parent object |
|`widgets/json-val.js` |`widget` |`<$json-val>` — pushes value to parent array, supports child-capture |
|`widgets/json-item.js` |`widget` |`<$json-item>` — pushes coerced scalar to parent array |
|`widgets/json-emit.js` |`widget` |`<$json-emit>` — renders JSON tree as text node |
|`widgets/json-save.js` |`widget` |`<$json-save>` — writes JSON tree to tiddler field |
|`widgets/json-debug.js` |`widget` |`<$json-debug>` — dumps warnings and raw tree |

!! Restart rules

|!Change |!Restart needed? |
|Any `.js` widget file |Yes — JS modules load at boot |
|Doc/readme `.tid` files |Yes — plugin shadow tiddlers |

<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/callout" type="info">
<$fill $name="body">
JSON DSL is entirely browser-side. "Restart" means restarting the TiddlyWiki server so the updated plugin shadow tiddlers are loaded. No server-side modules exist.
</$fill>
</$transclude>

!! Testing

Use `<$json-obj debug="yes">` with `<$json-debug/>` to see the assembled tree and any warnings. Warnings include issues like setting a property on an array or pushing a value without a parent container.

</$fill>
</$transclude>
